 {"id":"560fbf09-026a-4a2c-8127-805bf248c045","agency_id":"b67bb03f-bcf1-419e-83a2-224964147e34","title":"Mack Video 23","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1w9B_cnopKg1DWNUQfx2tB-TT77NjTV-P?usp=drive_link\"&gt;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1w9B_cnopKg1DWNUQfx2tB-TT77NjTV-P?usp=drive_link&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","status":"in_progress","client_id":null,"due_date":"2026-08-07T19:00:00+00:00","budget":null,"created_at":"2026-08-05T05:24:40.598326+00:00","updated_at":"2026-08-06T09:48:12.365538+00:00","editor_rate":null,"completed_at":null,"reference_links":null,"container_id":"a8baf896-777e-4bca-a451-b0bfe75bad7d","managed_client_id":"2015c089-44f4-4a3c-9ef0-d88d7a33202a"}, 
 {"id":"f424eaaf-ff0a-4979-9f56-f9af6d5e33eb","agency_id":"b67bb03f-bcf1-419e-83a2-224964147e34","title":"Mack Video 16","description":"&lt;p&gt;https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1426Cw3D5DTcawYYDRPwHY668dWHzYxOZ&lt;/p&gt;","status":"done","client_id":null,"due_date":"2026-07-11T19:00:00+00:00","budget":null,"created_at":"2026-07-11T09:12:13.998322+00:00","updated_at":"2026-07-18T05:54:57.435906+00:00","editor_rate":null,"completed_at":"2026-07-18T05:54:57.435906+00:00","reference_links":null,"container_id":"a8baf896-777e-4bca-a451-b0bfe75bad7d","managed_client_id":"2015c089-44f4-4a3c-9ef0-d88d7a33202a"}, 
 {"id":"023f2e2a-a0f1-4e5b-91b5-5b90ea7f7ef5","agency_id":"b67bb03f-bcf1-419e-83a2-224964147e34","title":"Christaugonus Video 3","description":"&lt;p&gt;Still not perfect but this editing is in right direction, the visuals frequently still behave like illustrations of the narration rather than scenes with their own internal progression. Shots around 1:17–1:22 and 2:03–2:08, for example, hold on archival imagery with limited movement. nearly every shot moves similarly, you need to add Static archival images with slow push-in or layered parallax. Never dead-flat, never fast zoom.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scary Interesting adds:&lt;br&gt;Foreground/background separation&lt;br&gt;Artificial camera depth&lt;br&gt;More pronounced lighting and texture&lt;br&gt;Red visual accents&lt;br&gt;Stronger transitions between narrative phases&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Graphics that would elevate video editing&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Typewritten FDA case-file captions&lt;br&gt;Red evidence circles and underlines&lt;br&gt;Animated shipment maps&lt;br&gt;Chemical diagrams connecting diethylene glycol to kidney failure&lt;br&gt;“633 SHIPMENTS” filling the frame&lt;br&gt;A split graphic contrasting ELIXIR with SOLUTION&lt;br&gt;Massengill’s “no responsibility” quote presented like a damning document exhibit&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sound design&lt;br&gt;Both videos use restrained sound, but yours feels flatter. you needed to add subtle, realistic layers:&lt;br&gt;Glass-bottle handling&lt;br&gt;Laboratory room tone&lt;br&gt;Telegram/typewriter sounds&lt;br&gt;Train ambience during the nationwide search&lt;br&gt;Paper movement under quoted letters&lt;br&gt;A low impact when “105 people” appears&lt;br&gt;Silence before Massengill’s statement at 7:27&lt;br&gt;Avoid constant horror hits. Four or five carefully designed moments would be more effective.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;# Editing Style Bible&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;One page. Check every video against it before export.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;**The rule in one line:---&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;## 1. Palette&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;RoleHexUsageBase black&lt;code&gt;#0a0805&lt;/code&gt;Backgrounds, vignette edges. Never pure #000.Sepia shadow&lt;code&gt;#3a2a14&lt;/code&gt;Photo shadows, dark midsSepia mid&lt;code&gt;#6b4a26&lt;/code&gt;The dominant archival toneWarm highlight&lt;code&gt;#8a7a5c&lt;/code&gt;Photo highlightsParchment&lt;code&gt;#c9bfa8&lt;/code&gt;Paper texture, document shots, light areas&lt;strong&gt;Danger red&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;#a01010#d32f2f&lt;/code&gt;RESERVED — see rule belowCold teal shadow&lt;code&gt;#203f3f&lt;/code&gt;Death/horror beats onlyCold teal mid&lt;code&gt;#456b6b&lt;/code&gt;Death/horror beats only&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Red rule:&lt;/strong&gt; red appears ONLY when the poison, the death count, or the lie is on screen. Title cards, key stats, the killer detail. If red is on screen more than ~10% of runtime, we've diluted it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cold-shift rule:&lt;/strong&gt; the teal grade is an &lt;em&gt;event&lt;/em&gt;, not a default. Drain to cold for the death montage / body horror beat, return to sepia after. One or two shifts per video, max.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;## 2. Shots &amp;amp; Pacing&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Static archival images with &lt;strong&gt;slow push-in or layered parallax&lt;/strong&gt;. Never dead-flat, never fast zoom.&lt;br&gt;- Shot length breathes with the act — pacing is the emotional instrument:&lt;br&gt;- &lt;strong&gt;Discovery / exposition:&lt;/strong&gt; 5–7s holds, gentle dissolves&lt;br&gt;- &lt;strong&gt;Escalation (deaths mount, hunt begins):&lt;/strong&gt; 3–4s, harder cuts&lt;br&gt;- &lt;strong&gt;Revelation:&lt;/strong&gt; one long held shot (7s+) on the key image, then release&lt;br&gt;- Never let the same image-push-dissolve pattern run more than ~4 shots without a pattern break (graphic, cold shift, cut to black, silence).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;## 3. Graphics&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Names, dates, place cards, circles/underlines on documents, medical terms — &lt;strong&gt;only when they clarify narration&lt;/strong&gt;. Not a caption stream.&lt;br&gt;- Manhunt/journey sequences get an &lt;strong&gt;animated map&lt;/strong&gt; (locations + connecting lines, sepia-styled).&lt;br&gt;- Big numbers get a &lt;strong&gt;stat card&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g. \"240 GALLONS / 633 SHIPMENTS / 239 INSPECTORS\") — parchment background, red for the deadly figure.&lt;br&gt;- Typography: one condensed display face for titles (distressed, as in thumbnails), one clean face for cards. No third font.&lt;br&gt;- Never screenshot a modern article/webpage as B-roll. Rebuild it as a period-styled document.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;## 4. Sound&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Target &lt;strong&gt;-14 LUFS integrated&lt;/strong&gt;, but loudness range (LRA) should be &lt;strong&gt;≥ 4 LU&lt;/strong&gt; — dynamics are mandatory. (Elixir video shipped at 1.8 LU: too flat.)&lt;br&gt;- &lt;strong&gt;Silence before every major reveal.&lt;/strong&gt; Music fully out for 1–3s, then the line lands. Minimum one true silence per video.&lt;br&gt;- &lt;strong&gt;Per-story environmental bed&lt;/strong&gt;, low in the mix and specific: pharmacy glass/paper for Elixir, volcanic hiss for Owakudani, jungle for the Congo story. One bed per story, established in the first 30s of that story.&lt;br&gt;- Music dips under emotional documents (letters, quotes) — narration nearly dry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;## 5. Openings &amp;amp; Endings&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cold open: narration begins within -3s. Optional 5 - 8s rapid flash-forward montage (ominous imagery, red text) is allowed before it, never delaying the first line past that.&lt;br&gt;Hook structure: horror first - systemic absurdity as the kicker (\"...and it was perfectly legal\").&lt;br&gt;Title card after the hook (~25–30s in), distressed type, red on black + archival image.&lt;br&gt;Ending: closing line lands (\"...a dark, silent hazard of history\"), then 5–10s of air, held image, music resolving. Never cut dead on the last word.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;## 6. Pre-export checklist&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- [ ] Red on screen only for danger beats&lt;br&gt;- [ ] At least one cold-shift event, returned to sepia&lt;br&gt;- [ ] No identical pacing pattern &amp;gt; 4 consecutive shots&lt;br&gt;- [ ] Map or stat card in any journey/numbers sequence&lt;br&gt;- [ ] One true silence before the biggest reveal&lt;br&gt;- [ ] Story-specific ambient bed present, LRA ≥ 4 LU&lt;br&gt;- [ ] Drug names / proper nouns pronounced correctly (listen back at 1x)&lt;br&gt;- [ ] 5–10s of air after the closing line&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pls checkout this video, I want same style of visual with reds circles and letters overlay, style but not the long static image narration. Motions and map&lt;a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gawm1TVslVs\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;https://&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gawm1TVslVs\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;www.youtube.com/watch?v=gawm1TVslVs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","status":"paid","client_id":null,"due_date":"2026-07-20T19:00:00+00:00","budget":null,"created_at":"2026-07-18T05:50:47.497585+00:00","updated_at":"2026-07-30T17:26:36.870579+00:00","editor_rate":null,"completed_at":null,"reference_links":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gawm1TVslVs","container_id":"2efe9af2-ee9f-48fc-8605-96c8f738b5e6","managed_client_id":"08998573-cd5c-45b9-9de8-37e3b17a9269"}, 
